      "statusChangeID": "5f0d42d6f5e3f7759eb0d5f5",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "This is the choice of the world/map creator, not of VRChat. \nIf the camera near-clip plane is too short and your avatar is too small, your mesh will begin to \"clip out\" when you move parts of it close to your viewpoint.\nThe solution is for the map author to lower the near-clip value for the reference camera, or for you to make your avatar larger. VRChat does not have control over this value in worlds.\nAs such, this cannot be a feature to request, and will be closed.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
